WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.563
Captain's Log:
Stardate 42609.1.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:09.666
In response to a desperate
plea from my old friend

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.576
Captain Donald Varley
of the USS Yamato

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.070
I am running a grave risk
by taking the Enterprise

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.606
into the Neutral Zone.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.949
Varley's request was prompted
by dangerous malfunctions

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.784
which have been plaguing
our sister ship.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.950
Perhaps with both crews
working together

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.857
we can eliminate the problems

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.522
before our presence is detected
by the Romulans.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:36.001
How long to rendezvous,
Mr. Crusher?

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:39.197
Four minutes
and 33 seconds, sir.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.706
Status of download, Mr. Data?

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.139
The Yamato log

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.700
should be in our computer
by rendezvous, sir.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.712
Have you nailed down
our little hiccup yet?

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.713
Sir?

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.374
The odd reading?

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.883
No, sir.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.475
It might be due to problems

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.010
currently being experienced
by the Yamato.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.555
Trouble, Number One?

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.715
I'm not sure, sir.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.019
Are we alone out here, Worf?

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.720
Yes, sir.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.093
There are no other vessels
in the area except the Yamato

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.325
which is coming
into visual range now.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.334
At last.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.330
Transmission
from the Yamato, sir.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.101
On viewer.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.507
Donald, what's a nice
Starfleet Captain like you

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.638
doing in a place like this?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.672
It's good to see you again,
Jean-Luc

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.980
despite your antique humor.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:29.112
I only hope your people
are able to help us.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:32.352
The malfunctions
are becoming serious.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.826
We lost an engineering team

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.261
when the computer shut down
a force field

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.958
in an open shuttle bay.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.865
18 People.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.234
Do you have any idea
what caused this, sir?

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.465
None.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.701
They're affecting every system
simultaneously.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.335
It's like the ship has suddenly
decided to fall apart.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.106
It's beginning to make me think

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.546
that we should have run
these galaxy class ships

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.244
across a few more drawing boards
before building one.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.718
You believe it's a design flaw?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.879
I don't know.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.048
I'm grasping at straws here.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.115
All I know is,
we've got to get it fixed

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.627
and before I lose more
than an engineering team.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.221
Do you wish to evacuate
any non-essential personnel

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.731
to the Enterprise,sir?

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.098
No. No, that would be premature.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.071
Donald, we'll get our teams
to work on it immediately.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.471
I'm sure neither of us
feels too comfortable

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.408
sitting around
in the Neutral Zone.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.536
I know what you're thinking--

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.739
what the hell am I doing here?

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.077
Well, I heard a...

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:32.676
a few rumors about
a couple of archaeological digs

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:37.179
that started making the lconians
sound a lot less like legend.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:41.182
I did a little investigating
and I located their homeworld.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.956
In the neutral zone?

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.861
In the neutral zone.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:47.196
Donald, that was quite
a risk to run

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.259
to satisfy
archaeological curiosity.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:56.264
The risk would be in allowing
the Romulans to locate lconia.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.877
Fortunately, I got there first.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:05.351
It's a virtually dead planet,
but enough technology remains

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:09.321
to give the Romulans an edge
if they should find it.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.190
Donald, your transmission
is breaking up.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.718
Mr. Data, try and clean that up.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.628
Sir, there is an energy build-up

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.724
in the Yamato's
engineering section.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:24.965
Yamato, this is the Enterprise.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.768
Yamato, come in.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:31.641
Captain, magnetic seals in the
antimatter chamber are decaying.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:32.975
Captain.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.309
Donald

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.907
Come in.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.280
Shields up.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.117
Sir.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.655
Sensors indicate...

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:55.190
no life reading, sir.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:02.037
Captain.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:05.943
Another vessel is coming
within sensor range.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.707
It is Romulan.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:34.906
Space, the final frontier.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:38.775
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.779
Its continuing mission--

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:44.749
to explore
strange new worlds

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:49.221
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:53.749
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.548
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:55.486
The Yamato's entire crew
and their families

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.388
more than a thousand people,
have been lost.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.415
Circumstances, unfortunately

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.293
permit us no pause for grief.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:05.923
No response from
the Romulan vessel.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.229
Arm phasers and prepare
to lock on target.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.327
Did they attack the Yamato?

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.669
Unknown, sir.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.607
All their weapons systems
have been fully activated.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.076
Still no response.

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:22.946
Romulan vessel, this is
Captain Jean-Luc Picard

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.914
of the USS Enterprise.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.012
Captain Picard.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.918
Explain your illegal presence
in the Neutral Zone.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.360
Explain yours.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:39.627
Are you responsible for the
destruction of the Yamato?

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.259
No, but believe me, Captain

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.099
had we chosen
to exercise our right

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:47.436
to defend the Neutral Zone

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:51.102
we would not have stopped
with one starship.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.237
You will leave at once.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.876
Mute.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:58.941
Comments?

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.145
She's extremely anxious.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:03.087
Understandable if she just
destroyed a Federation starship.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.487
Your scan was inconclusive.

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:07.118
We don't know what happened
to the Yamato.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.618
Our presence in the Neutral Zone
is provocative.

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.257
It could force her to respond.

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.065
Open.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:20.402
We will comply

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.499
when I have determined the cause

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.305
of the destruction
of the Yamato

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:27.744
and when I am fully satisfied
that you were not responsible.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.974
Picard out.

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.778
They're engaging
their cloaking device.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.946
Good.

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:36.750
They can't fire
when they're cloaked.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.916
Unless they have overcome
that deficiency.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:42.621
The Yamato was destroyed
while they were cloaked.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:43.754
Enough.

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:44.854
Answers.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.694
I want answers, not conjecture.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.292
Number One, I want them at
a staff meeting in one hour.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.529
Aye, sir.

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.968
Sensor recordings reveal

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:59.045
that what we witnessed
was an uncontrolled

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:02.204
and catastrophic
matter/antimatter mix.

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:06.378
The magnetic seals between
the chambers collapsed and...

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:07.443
Wait, wait.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.511
That's not possible.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:13.184
Yes, sir, it is, but a highly
improbable set of circumstances

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.625
has to take place
for such a result to occur.

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:17.720
Explain.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:21.221
Okay. In the event of a breach
of seal integrity

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.758
there's an emergency
release system

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:25.737
which dumps the antimatter.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.103
Apparently, such a dump
began, was then halted

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.836
and the containment
seals were dropped.

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:33.436
There was still sufficient
antimatter present

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:34.673
to lead to an explosion.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:37.648
And so there is no evidence
that a weapon was used?

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:38.911
No, sir, none.

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.418
However it happened

00:08:40.453 --> 00:08:42.944
the Yamato did it to herself.

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:44.421
Theorize.

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:49.121
What could have caused such
a catastrophic malfunction?

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:52.096
Well, I think Captain Varley
may have been right.

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:54.395
There may be a design flaw.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:56.094
In a galaxy class starship?

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.432
Yes, sir.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.405
It's the most sophisticated
piece of machinery ever built.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.304
Something could have
been overlooked.

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:05.037
Knowing where
the flaw is located

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.409
can you isolate the problem
and solve it?

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.778
We're already working
on it, sir.

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.908
Pull any personnel you can use.

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:15.713
If we have established

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:18.120
that the Romulans
were not responsible

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.819
for the destruction
of the Yamato

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.761
would it not be prudent
to withdraw?

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:28.062
If it is a design flaw,
we better stay where we are

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.069
and give Geordi time
to work on it

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:35.403
or what happened to the Yamato
could happen to us.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:56.952
Computer, access Captain
Donald Varley's personal log.

00:09:56.996 --> 00:10:00.932
Search parameter--
locate entries

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:06.268
containing words "Romulan"
and/or "lconian."

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:09.433
Working.

00:10:09.475 --> 00:10:10.942
Personal log.

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:14.776
It was kind of Dr. Ramsey
to allow me to carry away

00:10:14.813 --> 00:10:16.906
my own little piece of legend

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:20.146
from the archaeological dig
on Denius lll.

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:23.280
My engineers have examined it

00:10:23.322 --> 00:10:28.123
but are completely baffled
by its technology.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.628
What was its purpose?

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:34.656
I'm like the caveman
confronted by a tricorder.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.464
I'm certain this device
is lconian

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:39.801
but how far had it traveled

00:10:39.838 --> 00:10:43.467
before it was abandoned
on this alien world?

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.307
Personal log.

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:49.644
A galactic Rosetta stone.

00:10:49.682 --> 00:10:53.243
The starfields on the artifact
were unintelligible

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:57.813
until I took into account
200 millennia of stellar drift.

00:10:57.856 --> 00:11:01.223
After that it was easy
to pinpoint lconia.

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:05.756
My first officer is questioning
the wisdom of my order

00:11:05.798 --> 00:11:08.130
to violate the Neutral Zone

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:12.467
but I'm convinced that I've
taken the only proper course.

00:11:12.504 --> 00:11:14.665
Should this advanced technology

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.073
fall into the hands
of the Romulan

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:19.270
we might as well dock our ships

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:21.609
and defend ourselves
with sticks.

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:22.773
Personal log.

00:11:22.815 --> 00:11:25.613
We've been spotted
by a Romulan cruiser

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:27.710
but after playing hide and seek

00:11:27.753 --> 00:11:30.119
through several solar systems

00:11:30.155 --> 00:11:32.988
I think I've managed
to elude them.

00:11:33.993 --> 00:11:36.461
The lconian probe scan--

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:40.158
was it an attempt
at communication?

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:45.637
If only I knew
what we were dealing with here.

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:46.729
Personal log.

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:49.798
I'm unable to send an away team
to the surface of lconia

00:11:49.842 --> 00:11:53.642
nor can I scan
the energy source on the planet

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:56.477
because of
these maddening system failures.

00:11:56.515 --> 00:12:00.417
It's infuriating to be stopped
at the threshold of a dream

00:12:00.452 --> 00:12:02.249
by one's own ship.

00:12:02.288 --> 00:12:05.587
We're leaving orbit
to rendezvous with Picard.

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:08.718
If his people can't help us
repair the Yamato

00:12:08.761 --> 00:12:13.095
I must convince him
to continue this exploration.

00:12:13.132 --> 00:12:16.397
The future well-being
of the Federation

00:12:16.435 --> 00:12:18.767
may well depend upon it.

00:12:18.804 --> 00:12:20.965
No further entries

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:24.975
conforming to search parameters.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.433
Mr. Data

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:56.999
there was a reference
in Captain Varley's personal log

00:12:57.076 --> 00:12:59.408
to a probe that
scanned the Yamato.

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:02.243
Aye, sir, we have
the visual record.

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:04.772
Put it on main viewer.

00:13:05.918 --> 00:13:08.785
What the devil is that?

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:15.620
Have you seen anything

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:17.128
Iike that before?

00:13:17.162 --> 00:13:18.322
No, sir.

00:13:18.364 --> 00:13:20.195
It appears to be a scanner

00:13:20.232 --> 00:13:21.927
possibly a transmitter.

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:23.764
Transmitting what?

00:13:23.802 --> 00:13:25.201
Unknown, sir.

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:27.068
Engineering.

00:13:27.106 --> 00:13:28.266
La Forge.

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:30.434
What progress
on the matter/antimatter scan?

00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:32.103
Everything continues
to check out.

00:13:32.144 --> 00:13:35.580
I'm starting an analysis
on the magnetic coils.

00:13:35.614 --> 00:13:38.606
When the Yamato was probed,
where was she?

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.948
In orbit around a planet

00:13:40.986 --> 00:13:44.114
at coordinates 227
mark 359, sir.

00:13:46.992 --> 00:13:49.790
ETA at warp factor eight?

00:13:49.828 --> 00:13:52.991
12 hours, 16 minutes, sir.

00:13:53.098 --> 00:13:54.998
Sir, that would put us
substantially close

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:56.967
to the Romulan side
of the neutral zone.

00:13:57.002 --> 00:13:58.731
That can't be helped.

00:13:58.771 --> 00:14:00.102
Ensign, lay in a course.

00:14:00.139 --> 00:14:01.333
-Warp factor eight.
-Aye, sir.

00:14:01.373 --> 00:14:04.069
We're going to assume
the Yamato's mission.

00:14:04.109 --> 00:14:05.736
And risk a war?

00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:09.441
Or perhaps... prevent one.

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:19.883
Come.

00:14:22.094 --> 00:14:25.154
Sir, may I speak
with you a moment?

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:30.129
Yes, of course.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.599
Well, what is it, Wesley?

00:14:36.642 --> 00:14:39.406
It's about the lconians, sir.

00:14:39.445 --> 00:14:42.744
I was told they
were just a myth.

00:14:42.781 --> 00:14:47.081
China was thought to be a myth
until Marco Polo traveled there.

00:14:47.119 --> 00:14:49.917
No, the lconians
are certainly real.

00:14:49.955 --> 00:14:51.252
Sit down.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:54.782
We know that three systems
within this sector

00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:56.727
had a number of cultural
similarities

00:14:56.762 --> 00:14:59.128
similarities which
could only be explained

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:01.564
by there being
a single unifying influence.

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.500
So they colonized those worlds?

00:15:03.535 --> 00:15:05.867
Probably conquered.

00:15:05.904 --> 00:15:08.202
You mean they were warlike?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.707
Perhaps.

00:15:09.741 --> 00:15:16.146
Ancient texts did speak
of demons of air and darkness.

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.206
Air and darkness?

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.717
Legend has it

00:15:19.751 --> 00:15:23.881
that they traveled without
the benefit of spaceships

00:15:23.922 --> 00:15:25.719
merely appearing out of thin air

00:15:25.757 --> 00:15:27.554
on distant planets.

00:15:27.593 --> 00:15:29.185
Sounds like magic.

00:15:29.228 --> 00:15:33.722
Well, we would appear magical
to Stone Age people.

00:15:33.765 --> 00:15:37.326
How did you find all this out?

00:15:37.369 --> 00:15:42.068
Archaeology has been a hobby
of mine since Academy days

00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:47.044
but why don't we talk about
what really brought you here?

00:15:51.116 --> 00:15:54.347
It's the Yamato, Captain.

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:57.514
I can't stop
thinking about her.

00:15:57.556 --> 00:16:02.823
All those people...

00:16:02.861 --> 00:16:04.294
dead.

00:16:06.098 --> 00:16:10.194
I don't know how you and
Commander Riker and Geordi...

00:16:10.235 --> 00:16:11.930
how you handle it so easily.

00:16:12.004 --> 00:16:15.531
Easily?

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:18.236
Oh, no, not easily.

00:16:19.545 --> 00:16:22.180
We handle it because
we're trained to.

00:16:22.313 --> 00:16:25.043
As you will be.

00:16:25.082 --> 00:16:26.709
Tea. Earl Grey. Hot.

00:16:26.751 --> 00:16:29.549
But... if ever the time comes

00:16:29.587 --> 00:16:33.387
when the death
of a single individual

00:16:33.424 --> 00:16:35.449
fails to move us...

00:16:43.868 --> 00:16:45.768
Didn't you order tea, sir?

00:16:45.803 --> 00:16:49.068
Now, that should
not have happened.

00:16:49.106 --> 00:16:51.404
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:16:51.442 --> 00:16:54.172
As happened
with our sister ship

00:16:54.212 --> 00:16:56.305
the Enterprise is beginning
to experience a series

00:16:56.347 --> 00:16:58.110
of system failures.

00:16:58.149 --> 00:16:59.980
So far, they are random,
but I fear they could be

00:17:00.051 --> 00:17:01.814
early symptoms
of what happened to the Yamato.

00:17:01.852 --> 00:17:03.683
Engineering.

00:17:03.721 --> 00:17:04.915
La Forge.

00:17:04.956 --> 00:17:06.446
Lieutenant

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.050
are you making any progress
towards solving our problems?

00:17:09.093 --> 00:17:11.527
Solving them, no, sir,
but I can eliminate one worry.

00:17:11.562 --> 00:17:13.723
It is not a design flaw.

00:17:13.764 --> 00:17:15.288
I've been reviewing
the Yamato's log

00:17:15.333 --> 00:17:16.891
and I think that alien probe

00:17:16.934 --> 00:17:19.027
may have had something
to do with her problems.

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:20.037
How?

00:17:20.071 --> 00:17:21.663
I'd need to see the thing.

00:17:21.706 --> 00:17:24.607
If it was the probe,
that explains the Yamato

00:17:24.642 --> 00:17:27.440
But how do you account
for the difficulties

00:17:27.478 --> 00:17:29.469
the Enterprise is experiencing?

00:17:29.513 --> 00:17:31.037
I can't.

00:17:31.082 --> 00:17:35.109
Lieutenant, are our problems
likely to attain the seriousness

00:17:35.152 --> 00:17:36.881
of those on the Yamato?

00:17:36.921 --> 00:17:38.445
If you're asking for speculation

00:17:38.489 --> 00:17:39.888
I'd say yes, sir, they are.

00:17:39.924 --> 00:17:41.391
I need time.

00:17:41.425 --> 00:17:47.421
Mr. La Forge, time is one thing
we do not have in abundance.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:02.506
Analysis, Mr. Data?

00:18:02.546 --> 00:18:04.138
Scanning, sir.

00:18:10.721 --> 00:18:12.188
Well, Mr. Data?

00:18:12.223 --> 00:18:14.851
No life-form readings, sir.

00:18:14.892 --> 00:18:17.861
All major cities
have been heavily damaged

00:18:17.895 --> 00:18:19.260
and the pattern of destruction

00:18:19.297 --> 00:18:21.458
is that consistent with
large-scale orbital bombardment.

00:18:21.499 --> 00:18:23.023
How long ago?

00:18:23.067 --> 00:18:26.696
Approximately
200,000 years, sir.

00:18:26.737 --> 00:18:29.570
There is an energy source
in the mountains

00:18:29.607 --> 00:18:31.370
of the smaller continent.

00:18:31.409 --> 00:18:33.400
Magnify.

00:18:35.146 --> 00:18:37.546
Is that lconia?

00:18:37.581 --> 00:18:40.948
Captain Varley died
believing that it was.

00:18:43.254 --> 00:18:45.245
Did you see that?

00:18:45.289 --> 00:18:48.224
Captain, projectile launched
from the planet's surface.

00:18:48.259 --> 00:18:50.056
Its size and composition

00:18:50.094 --> 00:18:53.655
match the probe which scanned
the Yamato, sir.

00:18:53.698 --> 00:18:54.824
Shields up.

00:18:54.865 --> 00:18:56.355
Prepare a tractor beam.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:00.131
Mr. La Forge, I'm going to
assist you in your research.

00:19:00.171 --> 00:19:03.163
A probe has been launched
from lconia.

00:19:03.207 --> 00:19:05.539
I'm going to capture it.

00:19:07.378 --> 00:19:09.175
No, sir, wait!

00:19:09.213 --> 00:19:11.875
Captain! Captain!

00:19:21.225 --> 00:19:22.886
Coming through!

00:19:26.397 --> 00:19:27.557
Bridge.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.401
Emergency stop!

00:19:42.079 --> 00:19:43.706
Stop it, damn it!

00:20:06.771 --> 00:20:08.762
Tractor beam ready, sir.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:14.578
Geordi, are you all right?

00:20:14.612 --> 00:20:16.637
Destroy the probe, sir, quickly.

00:20:18.449 --> 00:20:20.280
Worf, target phasers.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.985
Phasers locked on target.

00:20:24.088 --> 00:20:25.077
Fire.

00:20:31.295 --> 00:20:33.923
Welcome to the Bridge,
Mr. La Forge.

00:20:33.964 --> 00:20:35.261
Thank you, sir.

00:20:35.299 --> 00:20:37.426
If that thing
had managed to scan us

00:20:37.468 --> 00:20:40.869
we never would have any chance
of saving the Enterprise.

00:20:46.043 --> 00:20:47.772
That probe was a transmitter

00:20:47.812 --> 00:20:49.541
sending
an alien computer program

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:52.640
the same program that is
currently aboard the Enterprise

00:20:52.683 --> 00:20:55.277
trying to rewrite our software
in its own image.

00:20:55.319 --> 00:20:58.186
We have two completely
incompatible computer systems

00:20:58.222 --> 00:20:59.712
trying to interact.

00:20:59.757 --> 00:21:00.985
So that's why
the ship's instruments

00:21:01.025 --> 00:21:01.992
have become so erratic.

00:21:02.026 --> 00:21:03.050
Yes.

00:21:03.093 --> 00:21:04.219
What can you do?

00:21:04.261 --> 00:21:05.387
Not very much.

00:21:05.429 --> 00:21:07.294
The lconian program
is so sophisticated

00:21:07.331 --> 00:21:08.764
I may never understand it.

00:21:08.799 --> 00:21:12.895
Consider Captain, this program
has entered an alien database--

00:21:12.937 --> 00:21:15.201
ours-- and in less
than seven hours

00:21:15.239 --> 00:21:18.140
has managed to not only
to learn our systems

00:21:18.175 --> 00:21:20.234
but has begun to reprogram
our computer.

00:21:20.277 --> 00:21:22.370
And so the earlier probe
was responsible

00:21:22.413 --> 00:21:24.244
for the Yamato's destruction?

00:21:24.281 --> 00:21:25.839
Yes, but only inasmuch

00:21:25.883 --> 00:21:28.852
as it was the probe
that transmitted the program.

00:21:28.886 --> 00:21:30.751
But we weren't scanned
by that probe.

00:21:30.788 --> 00:21:33.382
Then how did this thing
get aboard the Enterprise?

00:21:33.424 --> 00:21:34.891
We downloaded the Yamato log

00:21:34.925 --> 00:21:37.086
and contained in the log
was the program.

00:21:37.127 --> 00:21:40.221
Why didn't we suffer
the same fate?

00:21:40.264 --> 00:21:41.663
Well, the program affected

00:21:41.699 --> 00:21:43.530
all of the Yamato's systems
simultaneously

00:21:43.567 --> 00:21:45.194
but with us, it was deposited

00:21:45.236 --> 00:21:47.101
within a specific section
of our mainframe

00:21:47.137 --> 00:21:49.628
so it's having to work
it's way out from that location.

00:21:49.673 --> 00:21:51.971
That gives us
a little breathing space.

00:21:52.009 --> 00:21:54.307
Not much.

00:21:54.345 --> 00:21:59.373
The injury reports
are increasing, too, sir.

00:21:59.416 --> 00:22:02.476
Dr. Pulaski is unwilling
to trust the turbolifts.

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:05.819
She is sending medical teams
through the access tunnels.

00:22:05.856 --> 00:22:07.881
Captain...

00:22:07.925 --> 00:22:11.122
the Enterprise computer system
is a lot like our own bodies

00:22:11.161 --> 00:22:13.220
with voluntary
and involuntary systems.

00:22:13.264 --> 00:22:14.959
Now, probably
90% of what goes on

00:22:15.065 --> 00:22:16.896
in this ship
is done automatically

00:22:16.934 --> 00:22:19.129
completely out of our control.

00:22:19.169 --> 00:22:20.932
We're sitting on a bomb

00:22:20.971 --> 00:22:24.236
that could go off
any second or maybe never.

00:22:34.652 --> 00:22:36.711
The biobeds aren't working.

00:22:36.754 --> 00:22:38.745
The ship is falling apart.

00:22:38.789 --> 00:22:42.987
I've had 35 emergency calls
scattered across 12 decks.

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:47.360
My trauma teams are being
run ragged trying to respond.

00:22:47.398 --> 00:22:48.729
Biobeds!

00:22:48.766 --> 00:22:49.994
Dr. Pulaski.

00:22:50.100 --> 00:22:51.192
Yes?

00:22:51.235 --> 00:22:53.430
I've got a problem here.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.870
The knitter isn't working.

00:22:55.906 --> 00:22:57.464
Uh, try a splint.

00:22:57.508 --> 00:22:58.805
Doctor?

00:22:58.842 --> 00:23:00.810
Splint. It's a very
ancient concept.

00:23:00.844 --> 00:23:03.870
You take two flat pieces
of wood or plastic, a bandage.

00:23:03.914 --> 00:23:05.711
The broken limb
is kept immobile.

00:23:05.749 --> 00:23:08.240
That's crazy.
That's not practicing medicine.

00:23:08.285 --> 00:23:09.582
Oh, yes, it is.

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:11.815
It's a time-honored way
to practice medicine

00:23:11.855 --> 00:23:14.221
with your head,
and your heart and your hands.

00:23:14.258 --> 00:23:15.589
So jump to it.

00:23:17.761 --> 00:23:19.558
Damn.

00:23:19.597 --> 00:23:22.725
Try a bypass on the shield
control interface.

00:23:22.766 --> 00:23:24.233
No, no go.

00:23:24.268 --> 00:23:28.102
Let me see if I can directly
access the master program.

00:23:34.612 --> 00:23:35.670
Data.

00:23:35.713 --> 00:23:36.805
Yes?

00:23:36.847 --> 00:23:37.939
What happened?

00:23:37.982 --> 00:23:40.280
Any answer would be
mere speculation.

00:23:40.317 --> 00:23:41.807
This is yet another example

00:23:41.852 --> 00:23:44.286
of how our actions
have random results.

00:23:44.321 --> 00:23:45.345
Thanks, Data.

00:23:45.389 --> 00:23:47.584
I noticed.

00:23:47.625 --> 00:23:50.423
Life support has failed
on decks 7 and 13, sir.

00:23:50.461 --> 00:23:53.658
Now, what if this thing manages
to rewrite our entire system?

00:23:53.697 --> 00:23:54.994
It's so far beyond us

00:23:55.099 --> 00:23:57.294
we have no hope
of ever understanding it

00:23:57.334 --> 00:23:58.733
Iet alone controlling it.

00:23:58.769 --> 00:24:01.101
Our own ignorance could kill us.

00:24:01.138 --> 00:24:02.332
We may never...

00:24:02.373 --> 00:24:04.466
We may never reach that point.

00:24:04.508 --> 00:24:07.500
A variation of what
happened to the Yamato

00:24:07.544 --> 00:24:09.171
might destroy us first.

00:24:09.213 --> 00:24:12.444
So we just sit here and watch
our ship disintegrate around us?

00:24:12.483 --> 00:24:16.510
The probe was
launched from lconia

00:24:16.553 --> 00:24:20.580
probably
from an automated system.

00:24:20.624 --> 00:24:23.115
There may be records

00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:24.718
near the launch site

00:24:24.762 --> 00:24:27.196
that could help us
find a solution.

00:24:27.231 --> 00:24:30.758
I'll arrange an away team.

00:24:30.801 --> 00:24:32.632
And I'll lead it.

00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:34.467
You will lead it?

00:24:34.505 --> 00:24:36.530
Yes.

00:24:36.573 --> 00:24:38.473
Sir, we've had this conversation
100 times.

00:24:38.509 --> 00:24:40.443
And we will have it
again, Number One.

00:24:40.477 --> 00:24:44.379
I have been studying the
lconians since I was a cadet.

00:24:44.415 --> 00:24:46.406
I have to be the one to go.

00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:48.247
The Enterprise is yours.

00:24:48.285 --> 00:24:50.153
For as long as she lasts.

00:24:55.825 --> 00:24:57.816
I've got a lock
on the energy source

00:24:57.860 --> 00:24:59.725
and for the moment,
this baby's working

00:24:59.762 --> 00:25:01.491
but that could change
in an instant.

00:25:01.531 --> 00:25:03.055
We're aware of the risks.

00:25:03.099 --> 00:25:05.033
Energize.

00:25:13.509 --> 00:25:15.943
Transport complete.

00:25:15.978 --> 00:25:17.536
Stay sharp, Mr. O'Brien.

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:21.346
I want to be able to pull
them out at a moment's notice.

00:25:21.384 --> 00:25:22.578
Aye, sir.

00:25:22.618 --> 00:25:24.347
Commander, Romulan vessel.

00:25:24.387 --> 00:25:27.083
Open hailing frequencies.

00:25:27.123 --> 00:25:29.114
They're arming photon torpedoes.

00:25:29.158 --> 00:25:31.092
Shields up. Go to red alert.

00:25:31.127 --> 00:25:33.391
Sir, the shields
aren't responding.

00:25:33.429 --> 00:25:35.226
They're preparing to fire

00:25:35.264 --> 00:25:36.629
photon torpedoes.

00:25:36.666 --> 00:25:38.361
Mr. Crusher,
I need those shields.

00:25:38.401 --> 00:25:39.959
I'm trying, sir.

00:25:40.069 --> 00:25:41.263
They're firing.

00:25:51.547 --> 00:25:53.515
What happened?

00:25:53.549 --> 00:25:57.212
Instead of firing, they suddenly
disarmed and canceled.

00:25:57.253 --> 00:25:59.483
Fate.

00:25:59.522 --> 00:26:06.086
Protects fools, little children
and ships named Enterprise.

00:26:08.598 --> 00:26:11.931
Lock phasers on the Romulans
and hold your fire.

00:26:11.968 --> 00:26:14.198
Sir, the shields are back up.

00:26:14.237 --> 00:26:15.898
Impeccable timing.

00:26:15.938 --> 00:26:18.338
Sir, the shields
are back down.

00:26:18.374 --> 00:26:20.433
Phaser banks are down.

00:26:20.476 --> 00:26:22.341
Shields are back up.

00:26:22.378 --> 00:26:25.905
In another time and place,
this could be funny.

00:26:25.948 --> 00:26:28.178
Status of torpedo banks?

00:26:28.217 --> 00:26:30.515
They're down, too.

00:26:30.553 --> 00:26:31.884
If it should become necessary
to fight

00:26:31.921 --> 00:26:34.651
could you arrange to find me
some rocks to throw at them?

00:26:35.658 --> 00:26:38.183
Sir, the Romulan torpedoes
are continuing

00:26:38.227 --> 00:26:39.660
to arm and disarm.

00:26:39.695 --> 00:26:42.789
Perhaps its attempt
to fire was unintentional.

00:26:42.832 --> 00:26:44.629
Open hailing frequencies.

00:26:44.667 --> 00:26:45.929
Open.

00:26:45.968 --> 00:26:49.096
Romulan vessel, this is
Commander William Riker

00:26:49.138 --> 00:26:51.971
First Officer
of the USS Enterprise.

00:26:52.008 --> 00:26:54.374
Why did you attempt
to fire on us?

00:26:54.410 --> 00:26:57.311
This is Sub-commander Taris
of the Haakona.

00:26:57.346 --> 00:27:00.975
Why have you penetrated deeper
into the Neutral Zone?

00:27:01.050 --> 00:27:03.109
Why are you still here?

00:27:03.152 --> 00:27:06.178
I have claimed this planet
for the Romulan empire.

00:27:06.222 --> 00:27:07.814
This is the Neutral Zone.

00:27:07.857 --> 00:27:10.223
No one can claim anything.

00:27:10.259 --> 00:27:11.817
You will withdraw

00:27:11.861 --> 00:27:16.958
or I will be forced to destroy
your ship and your away team.

00:27:21.837 --> 00:27:23.930
What the hell...?

00:27:24.040 --> 00:27:26.770
This is your final warning.

00:27:26.809 --> 00:27:29.539
I will not...

00:27:29.578 --> 00:27:32.240
Having a little trouble
with your systems, Commander?

00:27:32.281 --> 00:27:35.876
Maybe we should consider
postponing the war

00:27:35.918 --> 00:27:39.479
until we solve our more
immediate problem.

00:27:39.522 --> 00:27:40.887
You're stalling for time.

00:27:40.923 --> 00:27:42.823
Sir, another probe launched
from the planet.

00:27:42.858 --> 00:27:44.951
Heading toward the Romulans.

00:27:44.994 --> 00:27:47.121
Have we got our phasers back?

00:27:47.163 --> 00:27:48.391
No, sir.

00:27:48.431 --> 00:27:50.490
Taris, if you have
phaser capability

00:27:50.533 --> 00:27:51.693
prepare to use them now.

00:27:51.734 --> 00:27:53.065
What?

00:27:53.102 --> 00:27:55.002
Destroy that probe.

00:28:06.549 --> 00:28:07.914
Not even a thank you.

00:28:07.983 --> 00:28:10.645
Sub-commander Taris
is deeply frustrated

00:28:10.686 --> 00:28:14.747
probably because her ship is
as crippled as the Enterprise.

00:28:14.790 --> 00:28:16.348
Why would the Romulans

00:28:16.392 --> 00:28:17.757
be experiencing problems?

00:28:17.793 --> 00:28:19.090
They weren't probed.

00:28:19.128 --> 00:28:21.187
They must have tapped
into the Yamato log.

00:28:23.032 --> 00:28:27.264
Taris got a whole lot more
than she bargained for.

00:28:27.303 --> 00:28:29.931
Maintain red alert

00:28:29.972 --> 00:28:32.236
and try to keep those shields up

00:28:32.274 --> 00:28:35.266
in case Taris decides
to act on her threat.

00:28:35.311 --> 00:28:36.608
Commander.

00:28:36.645 --> 00:28:38.135
What about the away team?

00:28:38.180 --> 00:28:40.978
With the shields up,
we can't beam them back.

00:28:49.325 --> 00:28:50.917
Captain's log, supplemental.

00:28:50.960 --> 00:28:53.190
While there is little left
on the surface of lconia

00:28:53.229 --> 00:28:55.459
we've found what appears to be

00:28:55.498 --> 00:28:58.194
a control center which seems
to have remained intact.

00:29:02.104 --> 00:29:03.799
Come in, Enterprise.

00:29:03.839 --> 00:29:07.536
Still no response, sir.

00:29:07.576 --> 00:29:08.736
Keep trying them.

00:29:08.778 --> 00:29:11.576
Communications are bound
to be erratic.

00:29:12.581 --> 00:29:14.742
I would not like to become

00:29:14.784 --> 00:29:17.514
a permanent resident
of this planet.

00:29:17.553 --> 00:29:19.384
Nor would l, Mr. Worf.

00:29:24.894 --> 00:29:29.058
Scanners show no other
life-forms on the planet, sir.

00:29:29.098 --> 00:29:31.089
I would not expect any.

00:29:31.133 --> 00:29:34.933
Judging from the severity
of the bombardment

00:29:35.004 --> 00:29:37.632
I doubt any lconians survived.

00:29:37.673 --> 00:29:39.038
Well...

00:29:39.074 --> 00:29:43.534
Mr. Data, let's see what sense
we can make of this.

00:29:43.579 --> 00:29:44.876
Aye, sir.

00:29:44.914 --> 00:29:47.940
This is very reminiscent
of Dinasian.

00:29:48.050 --> 00:29:49.517
Yes, sir.

00:29:49.552 --> 00:29:53.613
There are also similarities
to Dewan and lccobar.

00:29:53.656 --> 00:29:56.318
Is it possible they
could be branches

00:29:56.358 --> 00:29:58.223
of the same language family

00:29:58.260 --> 00:29:59.887
beginning with lconian?

00:29:59.929 --> 00:30:00.953
It is, sir.

00:30:01.030 --> 00:30:03.521
Run a comparison
using basic, simple words

00:30:03.566 --> 00:30:05.932
from Dinasian, Dewan,
and lccobar.

00:30:05.968 --> 00:30:09.870
Let's see if we can reconstruct
a common root language.

00:30:09.905 --> 00:30:11.270
Accessing, sir.

00:30:22.318 --> 00:30:24.411
You're jumpy.

00:30:24.453 --> 00:30:28.947
The tension on the ship
is very high.

00:30:32.027 --> 00:30:34.120
What's your recommendation?

00:30:34.163 --> 00:30:36.688
Give everyone something to do

00:30:36.732 --> 00:30:39.860
somewhere to focus
their attention.

00:30:39.902 --> 00:30:41.961
All right.

00:30:45.074 --> 00:30:47.269
Let's consider evacuation.

00:30:47.309 --> 00:30:49.140
To the planet?

00:30:49.178 --> 00:30:53.376
I know it's probably impossible
with Taris sitting out there

00:30:53.415 --> 00:30:56.680
but it would give everyone
something to do.

00:30:56.719 --> 00:30:58.186
You go and organize it.

00:30:58.220 --> 00:30:59.585
But you might need me

00:30:59.622 --> 00:31:01.920
if you have to negotiate
with Taris again.

00:31:01.957 --> 00:31:03.390
I'll manage.

00:31:03.425 --> 00:31:06.588
Right now,
they're more important.

00:31:18.607 --> 00:31:20.802
Captain.

00:31:20.843 --> 00:31:23.243
Your original hypothesis
is correct.

00:31:23.279 --> 00:31:26.646
Iconian is the parent tongue
of a language family

00:31:26.682 --> 00:31:29.810
which consists of lccobar,
Dewan and Dinasian.

00:31:29.852 --> 00:31:32.980
I've constructed a basic
working understanding

00:31:33.055 --> 00:31:35.785
through a comparison
of common root words

00:31:35.824 --> 00:31:39.988
such as mother, father, child,
home, tribe, food, life, death

00:31:40.095 --> 00:31:41.426
yours, ours, mine...

00:31:41.463 --> 00:31:42.760
Data, Data, Data.

00:31:42.798 --> 00:31:45.824
You do understand, sir, that
my interpretation of the symbols

00:31:45.868 --> 00:31:46.994
will not be exact?

00:31:47.102 --> 00:31:48.831
Yes, let's get on with it.

00:31:48.871 --> 00:31:51.738
This would appear to be
manual override.

00:32:03.419 --> 00:32:06.946
That was not manual override.

00:32:07.022 --> 00:32:10.788
Demons of air
and darkness, indeed.

00:32:14.063 --> 00:32:15.860
What is that?

00:32:15.898 --> 00:32:18.662
A gateway.

00:32:18.701 --> 00:32:21.431
These scenes could be
holographic images.

00:32:21.470 --> 00:32:22.494
Be careful.

00:32:25.741 --> 00:32:26.969
Data!

00:32:27.042 --> 00:32:29.067
That was very foolish.

00:32:29.111 --> 00:32:31.636
But we have established
this is not a holograph.

00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:33.409
If I step through
and investigate

00:32:33.449 --> 00:32:36.179
we could determine whether
this is truly a gateway.

00:32:36.218 --> 00:32:37.515
No, Data.

00:32:37.553 --> 00:32:39.680
You might not be
able to get back

00:32:39.722 --> 00:32:41.622
and I can't risk losing you.

00:32:41.657 --> 00:32:44.990
If it is not illusion,
this gate would seem to take us

00:32:45.027 --> 00:32:46.324
beyond the confines
of this planet.

00:32:46.362 --> 00:32:48.660
Is this how
the lconians traveled

00:32:48.697 --> 00:32:52.827
crossing light-years as easily
as we would cross a room?

00:32:52.868 --> 00:32:54.995
Those places could
be on worlds

00:32:55.037 --> 00:32:57.267
in distant corners
of the galaxy.

00:32:57.306 --> 00:33:01.003
I think the lconians might have
outfoxed their enemies.

00:33:01.076 --> 00:33:04.739
Maybe they didn't all die
in the bombardment.

00:33:04.780 --> 00:33:08.375
Some of them could have
passed through this.

00:33:08.417 --> 00:33:10.647
This is what Varley feared.

00:33:10.686 --> 00:33:12.210
This is what he died for.

00:33:12.254 --> 00:33:13.721
Sir?

00:33:13.756 --> 00:33:17.759
The Romulans could use
this technology as a weapon.

00:33:17.892 --> 00:33:19.450
Like the lconians did.

00:33:19.494 --> 00:33:20.961
No, I disagree.

00:33:21.028 --> 00:33:23.394
Captain, there is
nothing in this room

00:33:23.431 --> 00:33:27.629
to indicate it was used
as a military command center.

00:33:27.668 --> 00:33:29.795
Perhaps a transporter room.

00:33:29.837 --> 00:33:31.930
But the probe was hostile.

00:33:31.973 --> 00:33:34.407
We can't make that assumption.

00:33:34.442 --> 00:33:37.206
The effect on the Yamato
was devastating

00:33:37.245 --> 00:33:40.214
but what if it was
by accident, not by design?

00:33:40.248 --> 00:33:43.308
What I'm going to say
may sound unscientific

00:33:43.351 --> 00:33:46.377
but standing on this soil,
breathing in this air

00:33:46.420 --> 00:33:49.787
my instincts tell me
we may have got them wrong.

00:33:49.824 --> 00:33:52.315
But we do know
the lconians were conquerors.

00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:54.419
But that knowledge
was passed down

00:33:54.462 --> 00:33:57.625
by descendants of those
who attacked this world.

00:33:57.665 --> 00:34:01.396
The victors invariably write
history to their own advantage.

00:34:01.435 --> 00:34:04.700
There is an unfortunate tendency
in many cultures

00:34:04.739 --> 00:34:07.071
to fear what they
do not understand.

00:34:07.108 --> 00:34:09.269
It's possible
that their enemies

00:34:09.310 --> 00:34:11.244
confronted by this technology

00:34:11.279 --> 00:34:14.476
were driven to attack
the lconians out of fear.

00:34:15.483 --> 00:34:17.417
Sir.

00:34:24.258 --> 00:34:26.692
Was that really the Enterprise?

00:34:26.727 --> 00:34:28.922
I believe that it was.

00:34:28.963 --> 00:34:32.899
Gentlemen, we have a way home.

00:34:32.934 --> 00:34:36.335
Captain, there is a vast
underground power source

00:34:36.370 --> 00:34:38.270
which is controlled
by this console.

00:34:38.306 --> 00:34:40.968
I believe my triggering
of the gateway

00:34:41.075 --> 00:34:44.704
has caused a dramatic upsurge
in the power level.

00:34:44.745 --> 00:34:49.045
Ah, I have access.

00:35:08.102 --> 00:35:10.662
Data, can you hear me?

00:35:10.705 --> 00:35:13.196
Data, respond.

00:35:13.241 --> 00:35:15.573
Captain...

00:35:15.610 --> 00:35:17.737
Are you all right?

00:35:17.778 --> 00:35:20.212
No, I am damaged.

00:35:20.248 --> 00:35:21.875
How bad is it?

00:35:21.916 --> 00:35:25.545
The lconian program
is attempting to rewrite

00:35:25.586 --> 00:35:26.575
my software.

00:35:26.621 --> 00:35:28.384
Physical manifestations:

00:35:28.422 --> 00:35:31.186
blindness, motor con...

00:35:31.225 --> 00:35:34.752
Sir, without him,
we have no hope

00:35:34.795 --> 00:35:37.923
of deciphering the program.

00:35:39.333 --> 00:35:42.029
Captain, the Enterprise again.

00:35:45.573 --> 00:35:47.336
How long is the interval?

00:35:47.375 --> 00:35:50.139
About four minutes,
if the cycle holds.

00:35:50.177 --> 00:35:52.737
The next time
the Enterprise appears

00:35:52.780 --> 00:35:54.270
go through it with Data.

00:35:54.315 --> 00:35:56.510
Geordi will be able
to learn from him

00:35:56.550 --> 00:35:57.676
maybe help him.

00:35:57.718 --> 00:35:59.083
Sir, we have not yet established

00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:00.382
that that is truly a gateway.

00:36:00.421 --> 00:36:02.753
This will be the test.

00:36:02.790 --> 00:36:04.223
Aye, sir.

00:36:07.295 --> 00:36:08.819
Destroy the tricorder.

00:36:08.863 --> 00:36:11.263
Sir, it contains everything

00:36:11.299 --> 00:36:14.291
we've discovered
up to this point.

00:36:14.335 --> 00:36:17.099
And that is precisely
why it must be destroyed.

00:36:18.139 --> 00:36:19.902
How long?

00:36:19.941 --> 00:36:22.136
About three minutes.

00:36:22.176 --> 00:36:25.907
I'm running out of time.

00:36:25.947 --> 00:36:28.279
We all are.

00:36:28.316 --> 00:36:30.045
Data.

00:36:30.084 --> 00:36:33.747
Data, I have to destroy this.

00:36:33.788 --> 00:36:35.187
This control room

00:36:35.222 --> 00:36:36.780
and its technology
must not be allowed

00:36:36.824 --> 00:36:38.815
to fall into Romulan hands.

00:36:38.859 --> 00:36:40.190
I understand, sir.

00:36:40.227 --> 00:36:41.626
How? How do I do it?

00:36:41.662 --> 00:36:43.755
How do I destroy everything?

00:36:43.798 --> 00:36:46.995
The control room,
the probes, all of it?

00:36:48.903 --> 00:36:52.168
The power source, sir.

00:36:52.206 --> 00:36:54.902
I detonate it?

00:36:54.942 --> 00:36:57.502
How? How do I do that?

00:36:57.545 --> 00:36:59.706
The probes, sir.

00:36:59.747 --> 00:37:01.772
Probes?

00:37:01.816 --> 00:37:03.841
The probes.

00:37:03.884 --> 00:37:06.079
Launch?

00:37:06.120 --> 00:37:08.850
I launch the probes?

00:37:08.889 --> 00:37:11.084
Well... why?

00:37:11.125 --> 00:37:13.218
What good will that do?

00:37:13.260 --> 00:37:15.023
The doors, sir.

00:37:15.062 --> 00:37:16.927
Doors?

00:37:16.998 --> 00:37:19.466
Perhaps the probes
are in a launch bay.

00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.058
And if the doors are closed

00:37:21.102 --> 00:37:22.763
then the backwash
from the rockets

00:37:22.803 --> 00:37:25.863
will spill into the power grids
and there'll be an overload.

00:37:25.906 --> 00:37:26.930
Yes, sir.

00:37:27.041 --> 00:37:28.941
But the doors will
open automatically

00:37:28.976 --> 00:37:30.807
when the launch begins

00:37:30.845 --> 00:37:32.938
and I will override.

00:37:32.980 --> 00:37:34.811
Correct, sir.

00:37:34.849 --> 00:37:37.181
Which control keys?

00:37:37.218 --> 00:37:39.186
Damn.

00:37:39.220 --> 00:37:40.881
Of course, you can't see.

00:37:40.921 --> 00:37:44.584
Help...

00:37:44.625 --> 00:37:46.058
Worf, help him up.

00:37:50.865 --> 00:37:52.457
Describe, please.

00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:54.968
I'm standing directly
in front of the gate.

00:37:55.002 --> 00:37:58.369
To my left, there is
a small triangular screen.

00:37:58.406 --> 00:38:02.604
Right one meter.

00:38:02.643 --> 00:38:03.769
Right.

00:38:04.812 --> 00:38:07.713
Now, to my right
is a larger triangular screen

00:38:07.748 --> 00:38:09.443
to the top, is solid amber

00:38:09.483 --> 00:38:10.643
to the left, red.

00:38:10.684 --> 00:38:11.878
Correct.

00:38:11.919 --> 00:38:16.356
Key blue, amber, amber, red.

00:38:16.390 --> 00:38:18.255
That's the launch sequence?

00:38:19.794 --> 00:38:21.921
How do I override the doors?

00:38:21.996 --> 00:38:24.260
Blue, blue, blue.

00:38:24.298 --> 00:38:26.163
I hope that's not a stutter.

00:38:26.200 --> 00:38:27.724
I don't know how long a delay
there will be

00:38:27.768 --> 00:38:30.293
between the launch
and the detonation.

00:38:30.337 --> 00:38:32.931
I will hold keying
the launch sequence

00:38:33.007 --> 00:38:35.032
until you're through the gate.

00:38:35.076 --> 00:38:38.375
How long until
the Enterprise reappears?

00:38:38.412 --> 00:38:40.812
Almost time.

00:38:40.848 --> 00:38:44.944
Captain, you
will be killed.

00:38:45.052 --> 00:38:47.520
I'll go through the gate.

00:38:47.555 --> 00:38:49.455
But where will you end up?

00:38:49.490 --> 00:38:53.324
Very shortly, anywhere will
be preferable to this room.

00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:55.521
Mr. Worf, I am depending on you.

00:38:55.563 --> 00:38:58.430
You must get Data
back to the Enterprise.

00:38:58.466 --> 00:39:00.297
He may be their only hope.

00:39:00.334 --> 00:39:02.529
Aye, sir.

00:39:18.385 --> 00:39:19.852
Commander, look!

00:39:19.887 --> 00:39:21.218
Worf! What happened?

00:39:21.255 --> 00:39:22.586
Where's the Captain?

00:39:22.623 --> 00:39:24.853
We must take Data
to Engineering.

00:39:24.892 --> 00:39:28.225
Hopefully the Captain
will follow.

00:39:42.576 --> 00:39:45.238
I don't know how to help him,
but comparing

00:39:45.279 --> 00:39:48.339
recorded norms for Data
to these current readings

00:39:48.382 --> 00:39:51.840
it's clear that all his
functions are just going crazy.

00:39:51.886 --> 00:39:54.753
If we had an expert,
a Maddox, somebody, l...

00:40:08.102 --> 00:40:10.798
He's gone.

00:40:26.420 --> 00:40:28.980
Kandar we. Kandar pro.

00:40:29.056 --> 00:40:30.387
Kandar eja.

00:40:30.424 --> 00:40:32.984
Kandar stig.

00:40:33.027 --> 00:40:34.722
Kandar isay.

00:40:43.904 --> 00:40:45.496
Data!

00:40:45.539 --> 00:40:48.007
What the hell?

00:40:48.042 --> 00:40:49.839
I am accessing.

00:40:49.877 --> 00:40:53.574
The self-correcting mechanism.

00:40:53.614 --> 00:40:55.309
Captain?

00:40:55.349 --> 00:40:56.441
Captain!

00:40:56.483 --> 00:40:58.007
It's constantly kicking in

00:40:58.052 --> 00:41:01.419
to make minute adjustments
in the positronic brain.

00:41:01.455 --> 00:41:02.922
I am on the Enterprise.

00:41:02.957 --> 00:41:04.322
How did I get here?

00:41:04.358 --> 00:41:07.452
He cleared the lconian program
from his system-- how?

00:41:07.494 --> 00:41:08.961
Iconia...

00:41:08.996 --> 00:41:12.625
I was on lconia,
now I am on the Enterprise.

00:41:12.666 --> 00:41:14.566
Geordi, this is critical!

00:41:14.602 --> 00:41:15.967
How?!

00:41:16.003 --> 00:41:17.231
Okay, give me a second to think.

00:41:17.271 --> 00:41:18.533
There was an
incompatible program

00:41:18.572 --> 00:41:20.403
running through Data's system,
so the mechanism

00:41:20.441 --> 00:41:23.740
started searching for
a way to keep him alive.

00:41:23.777 --> 00:41:24.937
The solution...

00:41:24.979 --> 00:41:27.174
The solution was a shutdown

00:41:27.214 --> 00:41:30.342
and a total wipe
of all affected memory.

00:41:30.384 --> 00:41:32.579
Query. What have I forgotten?

00:41:32.620 --> 00:41:34.986
Can you do the same thing
with the Enterprise?

00:41:35.089 --> 00:41:36.556
I don't see why not

00:41:36.590 --> 00:41:38.387
but it will have to be
a complete shutdown.

00:41:38.425 --> 00:41:40.586
We turn her off, and effect
a wipe of the Yamato log

00:41:40.628 --> 00:41:42.994
including every subsequent event
since we downloaded it.

00:41:43.030 --> 00:41:45.191
I'll then be able to reload
all the ship's programs

00:41:45.232 --> 00:41:47.166
from the protected archives
in the main core.

00:41:47.299 --> 00:41:48.698
Geordi, if we shut down

00:41:48.734 --> 00:41:51.635
that means we're going to be
bringing down the shields

00:41:51.670 --> 00:41:55.003
and we're hanging nose to nose
with a Romulan battle cruiser.

00:41:55.040 --> 00:41:57.531
Hey, Commander, whether
it's Romulan phasers

00:41:57.576 --> 00:42:00.136
or our own warp engines,
we're just as dead.

00:42:00.179 --> 00:42:02.807
Make it so.

00:42:05.584 --> 00:42:06.949
May I help?

00:42:12.991 --> 00:42:15.186
Kandar neeah.

00:42:15.227 --> 00:42:17.661
Kandar goban.

00:42:17.696 --> 00:42:19.527
Kandar gonian.

00:42:24.970 --> 00:42:26.835
All systems functioning.

00:42:26.872 --> 00:42:30.103
Lock onto the Captain
and bring him back.

00:42:30.142 --> 00:42:31.575
Scanning, sir.

00:42:31.610 --> 00:42:33.271
Got him.

00:42:33.312 --> 00:42:34.677
Kandar get.

00:42:34.713 --> 00:42:36.112
Kandar say.

00:42:36.148 --> 00:42:37.706
Kandar por.

00:42:37.749 --> 00:42:39.478
Kandar aire.

00:42:39.518 --> 00:42:41.008
Kandar...

00:42:44.356 --> 00:42:47.985
Setha-tri par trukatha.

00:42:48.093 --> 00:42:50.357
Setha-ki par trukatha.

00:42:52.664 --> 00:42:54.131
I've lost him.

00:42:54.166 --> 00:42:55.565
Damn it!

00:42:55.601 --> 00:42:57.000
Got him, sir.

00:42:57.035 --> 00:42:59.094
He's on the Romulan ship.

00:42:59.137 --> 00:43:00.468
How the h...?

00:43:00.505 --> 00:43:03.338
Setha-mille par trukatha.

00:43:04.343 --> 00:43:07.403
Go to your stations.

00:43:07.446 --> 00:43:09.937
Setha-se par trukatha.

00:43:10.015 --> 00:43:11.915
Setha-ne par trukatha.

00:43:11.950 --> 00:43:15.113
Setha-ne par trukatha.

00:43:15.153 --> 00:43:17.485
You did this.

00:43:17.522 --> 00:43:19.717
You sabotaged my ship.

00:43:19.758 --> 00:43:21.350
Oh, no.

00:43:21.393 --> 00:43:24.521
I cannot deactivate
the auto-destruct

00:43:24.563 --> 00:43:27.657
but at least I have
the satisfaction

00:43:27.699 --> 00:43:30.224
that you will die with us.

00:43:30.269 --> 00:43:33.932
Not, I think, today, Commander.

00:43:36.642 --> 00:43:40.271
Setha-kargil par trukatha.

00:43:46.018 --> 00:43:47.315
Bridge, Picard.

00:43:47.352 --> 00:43:48.319
Yes, Captain?

00:43:48.353 --> 00:43:49.320
Take us out of here.

00:43:49.354 --> 00:43:50.981
The Romulan vessel is set
to auto-destruct

00:43:51.023 --> 00:43:52.320
and they can't deactivate.

00:43:52.357 --> 00:43:53.824
Wait, sir.
Open hailing frequencies.

00:43:53.859 --> 00:43:55.190
Open, sir.

00:43:55.227 --> 00:43:56.592
Commander Taris,
prepare to receive

00:43:56.628 --> 00:43:58.186
a transmission
from our chief engineer.

00:43:58.230 --> 00:43:59.993
He'll instruct you
how to purge your system.

00:44:00.065 --> 00:44:01.327
Agreed, Enterprise.

00:44:01.366 --> 00:44:02.731
Standing by.

00:44:02.768 --> 00:44:06.135
Commander, your transmission has
been received and acknowledged.

00:44:06.171 --> 00:44:08.196
Now, Mr. Data, warp speed,
please.

00:44:08.240 --> 00:44:10.333
Just in case Taris' engineer

00:44:10.375 --> 00:44:12.434
is not as efficient
as our Mr. La Forge.

00:44:12.477 --> 00:44:13.774
Aye, sir.

00:44:13.812 --> 00:44:15.439
Well, Number One

00:44:15.480 --> 00:44:19.280
I can see why you want to keep
the away missions to yourself.

00:44:19.318 --> 00:44:21.513
That's where the excitement is.

00:44:21.553 --> 00:44:24.317
So, what's been happening here?

00:44:24.356 --> 00:44:26.916
Same old routine, I suppose?
